    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d686">

                <pb facs="0927" n="857" xml:id="pg857"/>

                <head>The President of the United States to the Viceroy of Egypt.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1861-10-11"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 11, 1861.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Great and Good Friend:</hi> I have received from Mr.
                    Thayer, consul general of the United States at Alexandria, a full account of the
                    liberal, enlightened, and energetic proceedings which, on his complaint, you
                    have adopted in bringing to speedy and condign punishment the parties, subjects
                    of your highness in Upper Egypt, who were concerned in an act of criminal
                    persecution against Faris, an agent of certain Christian missionaries in Upper
                    Egypt. I pray your highness to be assured that these proceedings, at once so
                    prompt and so just, will be regarded as a new and unmistakable proof equally of
                    your highness’s friendship for the United States, and of the firmness,
                    integrity, and wisdom with which the government of your highness is conducted.
                    Wishing you great prosperity and success, I am your friend,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ABRAHAM LINCOLN.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Highness <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mohammed Said Pacha,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Viceroy of Egypt and its Dependencies, &amp;c.,
                            &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
                <postscript>
                    <p>By the president:</p>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
